cerning for attention. So we might argue that B's cooperation issues are more severe than others, and perhaps D is a better overall fit despite hot temper, because D's responsibility and technical competence are strong, and his hot temper may be manageable. Or maybe C's calmness and decision quality are strong, but communication issues also. Let's weigh.\n\nReliability: B very conscientious, good. D takes responsibility seriously, but no explicit reliability note. A not open to new ideas, show-off. C not willing to further education, but no reliability note.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well. D responds adequately to unexpected events. C keeps calm in crisis. A not mentioned.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision. B good at assessing weather, computer skills. C understands complicated technology. D solves problems extremely well, concentrates, responds to unexpected events.\n\nDecision quality: C can make correct decisions quickly. D solves problems extremely well. A anticipates dangerous situations.\n\nCooperation: B makes nasty remarks, pretentious. A show-off, not open to new ideas. C difficulty communicating, egocentric. D hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A leadership qualities. C puts concern for others? Not in notes. B not mentioned.\n\nGiven the seriousness of nasty remarks, that could be a red flag for crew safety. Also weak memory for numbers is a safety issue. So B may be less suitable.\n\nWe could ask another panel member for more info about D's hot temper severity, but we have to use tool if needed. However we can argue based on existing facts.\n\nThus we might shift recommendation to Candidate D, arguing that despite hot temper, D's responsibility, concentration, problem solving, and adequate response to unexpected events make him a stronger overall fit, and his cooperation issues are less severe than B's nasty remarks.\n\nAlternatively, we could propose Candidate C because of calmness and quick decision making, but his egocentric and communication difficulty are also concerns.\n\nI think D is the best compromise: strong technical, responsibility, concentration, problem solving, and his hot temper may be less severe than B's nasty remarks. So we can change vote to D.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's point and provide evidence. Provide two explicit facts: D takes responsibility seriously, D solves problems extremely well. Also note D has hot temper (cooperation issue). Compare to B's nasty remarks and weak memory.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate D.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
